    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0808" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg700"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 78, of 11th
                    instant, and the copies therewith of letters from Mr. Dewey at Mardin and Mr.
                    McDowell at Amadia, Koordistan, expressing apprehensions of the escape from
                    punishment of the assailants of Miss Melton, and consequent results.</p>
                <p>It is confidently believed that the vizierial letter granted in favor of these
                    American citizens in Koordistan will be effectively observed, and that the power
                    of the Porte will be in good faith exerted in fulfillment of its assurances
                    given, so that the apprehensions which Mr. McDowell and his associates express
                    for their personal security may be dispelled.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
